The first is "sea".
The second is "eat".
The firstsize is the number of characters in first.
The secondsize is the number of characters in second.
The width is secondsize plus 1.
The size is (firstsize plus 1) times width.
The table is a list of size zeros.
For every firstprefix from 1 to firstsize.
The cost is character (firstprefix minus 1) of first.
Set item (firstprefix times width) of table to item ((firstprefix minus 1) times width) of table plus cost.

For every secondprefix from 1 to secondsize.
The cost is character (secondprefix minus 1) of second.
Set item secondprefix of table to item (secondprefix minus 1) of table plus cost.

For every firstprefix from 1 to firstsize.
For every secondprefix from 1 to secondsize.
The index is firstprefix times width plus secondprefix.
The leftcost is character (firstprefix minus 1) of first.
The rightcost is character (secondprefix minus 1) of second.
The removal is item (index minus width) of table plus leftcost.
The insertion is item (index minus 1) of table plus rightcost.
The best is the smaller of removal and insertion.
If character (firstprefix minus 1) of first is character (secondprefix minus 1) of second, set item index of table to item (index minus width minus 1) of table.
Otherwise, set item index of table to best.

The last is one less than size.
Show item last of table.

